  "lyrics": "Gracious Spirit, dwell with me: I myself would\ngracious be, and, with words that help and heal,\nwould thy life in mine reveal, and, with actions\nbold and meek, would for Christ my Savior speak.\n\nTruthful Spirit, dwell with me: I myself would\ntruthful be, and, with wisdom kind and clear,\nlet thy life in mine appear, and, with actions\nlovingly speak my Lord's sincerity.\n\nSilent Spirit, dwell with me: I myself would\nsilent be, quiet as the growing blade,\nwhich through earth its way has made, silently, like\nmorning light, putting mists and chills to flight.\n\nMighty Spirit, dwell with me: I myself would\nmighty be, mighty so as to prevail\nwhere unaided I must fail, ever, by a\nmighty hope, pressing on and bearing up.\n\nHoly Spirit, dwell with me: I myself would\nholy be, break from sin and choose the good,\ncherish what my Savior would, and whatever\nI can be, give to him who gave me thee.\n",
